        "original_id": "ffe1b02a-5ed1-5126-95a8-1ffa31849bcb",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Events: 11th Academy Awards\n- Works: Grand Illusion, The Great Illusion\n- People: Jean Renoir, Norman Angell\n- Topics: Best Picture nominations, foreign-language films, anti-war ideas\n\nFacts:\n- At the 11th Academy Awards, Jean Renoir's film \"Grand Illusion\" became the first foreign-language film nominated for Best Picture.\n- The film \"Grand Illusion\" is also known as \"La Grande Illusion.\"\n- The title of \"Grand Illusion\" comes from \"The Great Illusion,\" a book by British journalist Norman Angell.\n- Norman Angell's book \"The Great Illusion\" argued that war is futile because European nations share common economic interests.",
